  intents: "command: fleet-axi intents\nusage: bin/fleet-axi intents [--days N] [--unlabelled] [--limit N]\n       bin/fleet-axi intents label <id> <owner>\nsummary: Jev's observe-mode verdicts on who should own each captain message to Alice (nothing is rerouted); label a verdict with the right owner to measure accuracy per confidence bucket\nflags[4]{flag,default,description}:\n  --days,7,how far back\n  --unlabelled,,only verdicts without a label\n  --limit,30,rows shown\n  --help,,show this help\nexamples[2]:\n  bin/fleet-axi intents --unlabelled\n  bin/fleet-axi intents label 12 architect",
  extract: `command: fleet-axi extract\nusage: bin/fleet-axi extract [--days N] [--unlabelled] [--limit N]\n       bin/fleet-axi extract run [--agent A] [--since DATE] [--dry-run]\n       bin/fleet-axi extract label <id> <label> [--target T]\nsummary: Jev's observe-mode proposals from the captain's own chat messages (nothing is written to captain.md or the facts; the strong recent ones queue in Needs you, and Remember / Not this there are the label, counted as accepted / dismissed here); run classifies the messages not yet seen, label sets the right class (${LABELS.join("|")}) to measure accuracy per confidence bucket\nflags[6]{flag,default,description}:\n  --days,7,how far back\n  --unlabelled,,only proposals without a label\n  --limit,30,rows shown\n  --agent,,run: one agent's chat only\n  --since,,run: only messages from this date or time\n  --dry-run,,run: list the candidates and the call count without calling Jev\nexamples[3]:\n  bin/fleet-axi extract run --dry-run\n  bin/fleet-axi extract --unlabelled\n  bin/fleet-axi extract label 12 preference`,
  proactive: `command: fleet-axi proactive\nusage: bin/fleet-axi proactive\n       bin/fleet-axi proactive snooze <fingerprint|key> <days>\n       bin/fleet-axi proactive done <key>\nsummary: What the node's sweep finds now (due within 2 days or overdue, closeable, stale task, stale fact, expiring observation) and whether Alice would be told, with the reason. snooze holds a finding for N days; done ends it until the thing itself changes (a new due date, another checked item). Proposals_30d counts what Alice reported, and the captain's Go, Snooze and Done on them, with the go rate per kind (the measure of whether this is wanted). A task untouched for FLEET_PROACTIVE_STALE_DAYS (21) is stale unless it waits on something. Mode is FLEET_PROACTIVE (observe by default; on gives Alice a turn).\nexamples[3]:\n  bin/fleet-axi proactive\n  bin/fleet-axi proactive snooze fleet-memory-m4 3\n  bin/fleet-axi proactive done fleet-memory-m4`,
  review: "command: fleet-axi review\nusage: bin/fleet-axi review <vault path> --writer <model> [--mode review|brainstorm] [--depth skip|light|full] [--lenses +comprehension] [--ship S]\nsummary: Asks the node for a survey of a vault note (fresh reviewers, each on its own model, never the writer's), waits for it, and prints the review file's path. Run it on the hub (bin/survey does, after syncing the vault). Without --depth, Jev decides; --depth is yours, skip included.\nflags[6]{flag,default,description}:\n  --writer,,the model that wrote the note, required; no reviewer shares it\n  --mode,review,review checks a draft; brainstorm fleshes out a raw idea or request\n  --depth,,skip, light or full (Jev decides when omitted)\n  --lenses,,+comprehension adds the naive-reader lens (review only)\n  --ship,,the ship whose code the draft is about (default: the note's ship: frontmatter)\n  --help,,show this help\nexamples[2]:\n  bin/survey fleet/plans/feature/x.md --writer anthropic/claude-opus-5.5\n  bin/fleet-axi review fleet/plans/feature/x.md --writer sol --depth full",
  setup: "command: fleet-axi setup\nusage: bin/fleet-axi setup hooks\nsummary: Add a SessionStart hook to .claude/settings.local.json (gitignored) that prints bin/fleet-axi --brief; running it again changes nothing, and so does a fleet-axi hook already in .claude/settings.json (the engineer's brief)\nflags[1]{flag,description}:\n  --help,show this help\nexamples[1]:\n  bin/fleet-axi setup hooks",
